SE: The 'this.options.subject' is assigned to the result of calling the html() method on a jQuery object that has had text() called on it with 'this.options.subject' as an argument. If 'this.options.subject' is user input that has not been properly sanitized, this could potentially result in Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability.
BL: this.options.subject = $('<div/>').text(this.options.subject).html();
BUG FOUND: YES

SE: The 'display\_name' and 'getLogin()' are directly concatenated into HTML content without sanitation.
BL: `$options .= sprintf('<option value="%d" %s>%s (%s)</option>', $userId, (($userId === $id) ? 'selected' : ''), $this->user->getUserData('display\_name'), $this->user->getLogin())`;
BUG FOUND: YES

SE: The 'svgString' variable is being manipulated and concatenated into HTML content without proper sanitation.
BL: svgString = svgString.replace('<svg ', '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" ');
svgString = svgString.replace(svgAttrs[0], svgAttrs[0].replace(/&ns_[^;]+;/g, 'http://ns.adobe.com/Extensibility/1.0/'));
svgString = svgString.replace(/\(<image[^>]+?xlink:href=["']\)data:img\/png/g, ($0, $1) => `${$1}data:image/png`);
svgString = svgString.replace(/(xmlns:(?!xml=)[^ ]+)="http:\/\/www.w3.org\/XML\/1998\/namespace"/g, ($0, $1) => `${$1}="http://dummy.namespace"`);
svgString = svgString.replace(/<metadata>[\s\S]*<\/metadata>/, '<metadata></metadata>');
svgString = svgString.replace(/<script[\s\S]*>[\s\S]*<\/script>/, '<script></script>');
svgString = svgString.replace(eventsRegex, '');
BUG FOUND: YES

Explanation:
The code manipulates an SVG string, which may contain user input, and concatenates it into HTML content without proper sanitation. This could potentially lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities if the SVG string is not properly sanitized.

